   "id": "pmt/pure-core-1/ch9/q4",
   "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:70mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/pmt/pure-core-1-ch9/q04-fig-1.png\" alt=\"Figure 1: tetrahedron ABCD with vertex A below a horizontal plane z = 0 (drawn dashed) and B, C, D above it; the edges AB, AC and AD cross the plane at M, N and P, and triangle MNP is drawn dashed in the plane\"></figure><p>The points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(3,2,-4)\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(9,-4,2)\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C(-6,-10,8)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D(-4,-5,10)\"></span> are the vertices of a tetrahedron.</p><p>The plane with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=0\"></span> cuts the tetrahedron into two pieces, one on each side of the plane.</p><p>The edges <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AC\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AD\"></span> of the tetrahedron intersect the plane at the points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> respectively, as shown in Figure 1.</p><p>Determine</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>the coordinates of the points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"N\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>, <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>the area of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"MNP\"></span>, <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>the exact volume of the solid <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BCDPNM\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol>",
