   "id": "pmt/pure-core-1/ch9/q6",
   "question": "<p>An octopus is able to catch any fish that swim within a distance of 2 m from the octopus's position.</p><p>A fish <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F\"></span> swims from a point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> to a point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span>.</p><p>The octopus is modelled as a fixed particle at the origin <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span>.</p><p>Fish <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F\"></span> is modelled as a particle moving in a straight line from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span>.</p><p>Relative to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span>, the coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-3,1,-7)\"></span> and the coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(9,4,11)\"></span>, where the unit of distance is metres.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Use the model to determine whether or not the octopus is able to catch fish <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></li><li>Criticise the model in relation to fish <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li><li>Criticise the model in relation to the octopus. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
   "steps": [
