   "id": "pmt/pure-core-1/ch9/q7",
   "question": "<p>Part of the mains water system for a housing estate consists of water pipes buried beneath the ground surface. The water pipes are modelled as straight line segments. One water pipe, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"W\"></span>, is buried beneath a particular road. With respect to a fixed origin <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span>, the road surface is modelled as a plane with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3x-5y-18z=7\"></span>, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"W\"></span> passes through the points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(-1,-1,-3)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(1,2,-3)\"></span>. The units are in metres.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Use the model to calculate the acute angle between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"W\"></span> and the road surface. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol><p>A point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C(-1,-2,0)\"></span> lies on the road. A section of water pipe needs to be connected to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"W\"></span> from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li>Using the model, find, to the nearest cm, the shortest length of pipe needed to connect <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"W\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol>",
