   "id": "pmt/pure-core-1/ch9/q8",
   "question": "<p>The plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\"></span> has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\3\\\\2\\end{pmatrix}+\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}-1\\\\2\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}+\\mu\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\0\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mu\"></span> are scalar parameters.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Show that vector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\mathbf i+3\\mathbf j-4\\mathbf k\"></span> is perpendicular to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Hence find a Cartesian equation of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=\\begin{pmatrix}4\\\\-5\\\\2\\end{pmatrix}+t\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\6\\\\-3\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> is a scalar parameter.</p><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> lies on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span>.</p><p>Given that the shortest distance between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\sqrt{29}\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"3\"><li>determine the possible coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
