   "id": "pmt/pure-core-1/ch9/q10",
   "question": "<p>A gas company maintains a straight pipeline that passes under a mountain.</p><p>The pipeline is modelled as a straight line and one side of the mountain is modelled as a plane.</p><p>There are accessways from a control centre to two access points on the pipeline.</p><p>Modelling the control centre as the origin <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span>, the two access points on the pipeline have coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(-300,400,-150)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q(300,300,-50)\"></span>, where the units are metres.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Find a vector equation for the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"PQ\"></span>, giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=\\mathbf a+\\lambda\\mathbf b\"></span>,<br>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda\"></span> is a scalar parameter. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>The equation of the plane modelling the side of the mountain is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x+3y-5z=300\"></span></p><p>The company wants to create a new accessway from this side of the mountain to the pipeline.</p><p>The accessway will consist of a tunnel of shortest possible length between the pipeline and the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M(100,k,100)\"></span> on this side of the mountain, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li>Using the model, find<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>the coordinates of the point at which this tunnel will meet the pipeline,</li><li>the length of this tunnel.</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></li></ol><p>It is only practical to construct the new accessway if it will be significantly shorter than both of the existing accessways, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"OP\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"OQ\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"3\"><li>Determine whether the company should build the new accessway. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Suggest one limitation of the model. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
   "steps": [
    "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/pmt/pure-core-1-ch9/q10-ms-p34-1.png\" width=\"890\" height=\"871\" alt=\"PMT mark scheme for Core Pure 1 Ch.9 Vectors Q10; source page 34, segment 1 of 4. Includes the working, marks, alternative methods and notes in source order.\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:100%\"></figure>",
