   "id": "pmt/pure-core-1/ch9/q11",
   "question": "<p>With respect to a fixed origin <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span>, the lines <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> are given by the equations</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"l_1:\\mathbf r=\\begin{pmatrix}4\\\\28\\\\4\\end{pmatrix}+\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}-1\\\\-5\\\\1\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad l_2:\\mathbf r=\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\3\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}+\\mu\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\0\\\\-4\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mu\"></span> are scalar parameters.</p><p>The lines <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> intersect at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Find the coordinates of the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>Find the size of the acute angle between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span>, giving your answer in degrees to 2 decimal places. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> lies on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and has position vector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\18\\\\6\\end{pmatrix}\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"3\"><li>Find the distance <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AX\"></span>, giving your answer as a surd in its simplest form. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Y\"></span> lies on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span>. Given that the vector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\overrightarrow{YA}\"></span> is perpendicular to the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"4\"><li>find the distance <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"YA\"></span>, giving your answer to one decimal place. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> lies on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|\\overrightarrow{AX}|=2|\\overrightarrow{AB}|\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"5\"><li>Find the two possible position vectors of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
